  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>Yaetil</defName>
    <label>raw yaetil</label>
    <description>A basic form of yaetilithic metal that has been artificially produced directly from the initial refining process without any further work done in refining it or removing impurities. This quality of Yaetil is similar in properties to copper with regards to its hardness and malleability, making it easy to cold hammer into a variety of shapes and forms, while also being sharp enough to be usable for cutting and chopping tools. That said, the impurities within the metal can cause pieces to break unpredictably, and also unlike copper it has a more "woodgrain" like structure as the yaetil formed around the impurities, often creating strands and ripple patterns of mineral impurities within the metal.</description>
