  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>Yaetil_Forged</defName>
    <label>forged yaetil</label>
    <description>A variant of yaetil that has been heated at least to 350 degrees Celsius and hammered. This hammering process, much like hammering a wrought iron bloom, can help eject impurities from the metal and homogenize the metal into a more solid, pure form. This, in turn, makes the metal harder, often being more comparable to a low quality wrought iron, being harder than copper though still not a terribly hard metal.</description>
