    <description>A variant of yaetil that has been melted at 500 degrees Celsius in a crucible, melting it. While melted in a crucible most of the impurities within the original metal will float to the surface and can be simply removed before pouring the molten metal into a mold. Smelted yaetil is the highest quality yaetil thanks to it often having no impurities remaining within it, often being comparable to a high quality tin bronze in hardness.</description>
